---
title: "buy_donut (Sui Move Concepts: Shared Object Interaction)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_payment: assert coin::value(payment) >= shop.price
    q_check_payment --> q_split: payment sufficient
    q_check_payment --> q_abort: payment insufficient
    q_split --> q_join: paid = payment.balance_mut.split(shop.price)
    q_join --> q_create_donut: shop.balance.join(paid)
    q_create_donut --> q_transfer: Donut { id: object::new(ctx) }
    q_transfer --> [*]: transfer::transfer(donut, ctx.sender())

    q_abort --> [*]: abort ENotEnough

    note right of q_check_payment
        INV-001: Payment must be >= shop.price to purchase
        INV-002: shop is a shared object - anyone can call buy_donut
    end note

    note right of q_split
        INV-003: Exact shop.price amount is split from payment coin
        INV-004: Remaining balance stays in caller payment coin
    end note

    note right of q_join
        INV-005: Shop balance increases by exactly shop.price
        INV-006: No funds are lost in the split-join cycle
    end note

    note right of q_transfer
        INV-007: Donut is transferred to transaction sender
        INV-008: Each donut gets a fresh unique UID
    end note
